{"name":"Magical Girl","title":"Magical Girl","revision":232873,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Magical_Girl","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Magical Girls are often in a team of young girls, destined to save the world. These characters often have their own designated color, weapon, and power assigned to them, although which colors, weapons, and powers can vary. Alongside these color coded costumes, a very iconic part of what makes a Magical Girl a Magical Girl visually is the animated transformation from a normal young girl into her Magical Girl identity."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Sally the Witch by Mitsuteru Yokoyama was the first Magical Girl anime to air in 1966, whilst Himitsu no Akko-chan was the first Magical Girl manga (first printed in 1962), but the most well known and influential Magical Girl anime in pop culture is Pretty Soldier Sailor Moon (often shortened to Sailor Moon) by Naoko Takeuchi."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Transformations"},{"kind":"list","text":"Glitter"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ribbons"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stars, hearts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Soft colors, often pink"},{"kind":"list","text":"School uniforms or anything like decorated dresses"},{"kind":"list","text":"90's anime"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wands, lockets, brooches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brightly Colored Hair"},{"kind":"list","text":"Animal companions"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Magical girl-inspired fashion, also known as Mahou Kei, shares many visual similarities with Fairy Kei. Beyond the casual outfits with magical girl print, there are also many frilly sailor uniforms and over-the-top Lolita dresses inspired by the outfits from the various series. Handmade transformation compact brooches and magic wands are popular accessories. Different to other styles, wigs are very common to be worn due to the extensive styling that gives a more otherworldly feeling to the outfit."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"Aikatsu!"},{"kind":"list","text":"Balala the Fairies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bee and Puppycat"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cardcaptor Sakura"},{"kind":"list","text":"Catch! Teenieping"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cute High Earth Defense Club Love!"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cutie Honey Flash"},{"kind":"list","text":"Corrector Yui"},{"kind":"list","text":"Creamy Mami"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fairy Tail"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fancy Lala"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fate/Kaleid Liner Prisma Illya"},{"kind":"list","text":"Flip Flappers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Flowering Heart"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fullmoon wo Sagashite"},{"kind":"list","text":"Himitsu no Akko-chan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Himitsu no AiPri"},{"kind":"list","text":"Idol Time PriPara"},{"kind":"list","text":"Is This A Zombie?"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jewelpet"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kamichama Karin"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kamikaze Kaito Jeanne"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lalabel, the Magical Girl"},{"kind":"list","text":"LoliRock"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lilpri"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maebashi Witches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Angel Sweet Mint"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Emi, the Magic Star"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Doremi"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Girl Friendship Squad"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Girl Pretty Sammy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Girl Raising Project"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Girl Site"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Princess Minky Momo"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magic Knight Rayearth"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mahou Shoujo Ore"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mermaid Melody Pichi Pichi Pitch"},{"kind":"list","text":"Moetan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Miraculous Ladybug"},{"kind":"list","text":"My-HiME"},{"kind":"list","text":